---
.title = "iroh: encrypted peer-to-peer",
.description = "iroh carries CapTP over encrypted QUIC with discovery and NAT traversal, and names each peer by a self-authenticating key rather than a host and port.",
.date = .date("2026-06-17T00:00:00"),
.layout = "page.shtml",
.draft = false,
---

iroh lets two peers find each other without a fixed address or a server in the
middle. A session's bytes travel over
[QUIC](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000.html), carried by
[iroh](https://www.iroh.computer/), and a peer is named by a key that proves
itself rather than by a `host:port`. Discovery, relays, and NAT traversal come
with the channel. The CapTP session on top is unchanged.
For a direct TCP route between glowcap peers that only needs encryption, prefer
[Noise]($link.page('transports/noise')) (`noise-tcp`) instead.

Goblins ships no iroh netlayer. Live Goblins-over-iroh
(`zig build goblins-iroh`) uses the adapter in `conformance/goblins-peer/`.
Prefer [onion]($link.page('transports/onion')) when both sides should run
unmodified upstream transports.

# Dial

These are the binding snippets again. The provider holds the configuration, and
each dial passes only the locator and any per-connect options.

```=html
<!-- site-examples:dial:iroh GENERATED by `zig build gen-site-examples`; edits are overwritten -->
```
> []($block.attrs('code-tabs'))
> **Zig**
> ```zig
> const std = @import("std");
> const glowcap = @import("glowcap");
> const iroh = @import("iroh");
>
> pub fn example(io: std.Io, allocator: std.mem.Allocator, partner_uri: []const u8) !void {
>     const partner = try glowcap.ocapn.model.uri.parsePeer(allocator, partner_uri);
>     defer glowcap.ocapn.model.freePeerLocator(allocator, partner);
>     var endpoint = try iroh.Resident.init(io, null, .{ .reachability = .discovery });
>     defer endpoint.deinit() catch |err| std.log.err("iroh endpoint: {s}", .{@errorName(err)});
>     var adapter = try iroh.MultiplexedAdapter.init(allocator, &endpoint);
>     defer if (adapter.deinit()) |failure| std.log.err("iroh adapter: {s}", .{failure.primaryName()});
>     const residents = [_]glowcap.driver.HostRuntime.ProviderRegistration{
>         .{ .profile = iroh.transport_profile, .resident = adapter.multiplexed() },
>     };
>
>     const session = try glowcap.driver.connect(
>         allocator,
>         io,
>         .{ .residents = &residents },
>         partner,
>         .ephemeral,
>         .{ .handshake = .{ .ms = 10_000 }, .settle = .{ .ms = 10_000 } },
>     );
> ```
> **TypeScript**
> ```ts
> import { Runtime } from "@glowcap/runtime";
> import { locator, provider, Reachability } from "@glowcap/iroh";
>
> // Discovery resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
> const nodeId = "<64 lowercase hex characters from the server>";
> const partner = locator(nodeId);
>
> await using runtime = await Runtime.open({
> 	providers: [provider({ reachability: Reachability.Discovery })],
> });
> ```
> **Browser**
> ```ts
> import { init } from "@glowcap/web";
>
> const web = await init({
> 	wasm: fetch("/glowcap_host.wasm"),
> 	relayUrl: (locator) => `wss://relay.example/?locator=${encodeURIComponent(locator)}`,
> });
> await using runtime = web.runtime;
> // `@glowcap/iroh` loads native FFI, so a page parses the locator on the web runtime.
> const partner = web.parseLocator("ocapn://<64 lowercase hex characters>.iroh");
> ```
> **Python**
> ```python
> from glowcap import Runtime
> from glowcap.iroh import IrohConfig, Reachability, locator, provider
>
> # DISCOVERY resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
> node_id = "<64 lowercase hex characters from the server>"
> partner = locator(node_id)
>
> async with Runtime.open(
>     provider=provider(IrohConfig(Reachability.DISCOVERY))
> ) as runtime:
> ```
> **Rust**
> ```rust
> use glowcap::iroh::{self, Reachability};
> use glowcap::{Argument, ConnectOptions, PendingWork, Runtime, RuntimeConfig};
>
> // Discovery resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
> // Cargo.toml: glowcap = { …, features = ["iroh"] }
> let node_id = "<64 lowercase hex characters from the server>";
> let partner = iroh::locator(node_id, None);
>
> let runtime = Runtime::open(RuntimeConfig::providers([iroh::provider(iroh::Config::new(
>     Reachability::Discovery,
> ))]))
> .await?;
> ```
> **Racket**
> ```scheme
> (require "glowcap.rkt"
>          "glowcap-iroh.rkt")
>
> ;; IROH-REACH-DISCOVERY resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
> (define node-id "<64 lowercase hex characters from the server>")
> (define partner (iroh-locator node-id))
>
> (define runtime
>   (open-runtime
>    #:providers (list (iroh-provider (make-iroh-config IROH-REACH-DISCOVERY)))))
> ```
